{"name":"Regatta Bay","hex":"#2d5367","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"regatta","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A series of boat races, or sometimes a single race.","A striped cotton fabric."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/regatta"},{"term":"bay","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Batuley."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A body of water (especially the sea) contained by a concave shoreline.","A bank or dam to keep back water."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bay"}],"entries":[{"title":"Boat racing","blocks":[{"text":"Boat racing (Regatta) is a sport in which boats, or other types of watercraft, race on water. Boat racing powered by oars is recorded as having occurred in ancient Egypt, and it is likely that people have engaged in races involving boats and other water-borne craft for as long as such watercraft have existed."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boat_racing","wikidata":"Q11344830"},{"title":"Bay","blocks":[{"text":"A bay is a recessed, coastal body of water that directly connects to a larger main body of water, such as an ocean, a lake, or another bay. A large bay is usually called a gulf, sea, sound, or bight. A cove is a small, circular bay with a narrow entrance. A fjord is an elongated bay formed by glacial action.\nThe term embayment is also used for related features, such as extinct bays or freshwater environments."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Aerial_photograph_of_Langness_and_the_bay_at_Castletown_13_February_2014_-_geograph.org.uk_-_3847162.jpg/330px-Aerial_photograph_of_Langness_and_the_bay_at_Castletown_13_February_2014_-_geograph.org.uk_-_3847162.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bay","wikidata":"Q39594"},{"title":"Bay (horse)","blocks":[{"text":"Bay is a hair coat color of horses, characterized by a reddish-brown or brown body color with a black point coloration on the mane, tail, ear edges, and lower legs. Bay is one of the most common coat colors in many horse breeds."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/BayMare.jpg/330px-BayMare.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bay_(horse)","wikidata":"Q900906"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Eights_at_Head_of_the_Schuylkill.jpg/500px-Eights_at_Head_of_the_Schuylkill.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Eights_at_Head_of_the_Schuylkill.jpg/500px-Eights_at_Head_of_the_Schuylkill.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Head of the Schuylkill Regatta","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEights_at_Head_of_the_Schuylkill.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Rowing%2C_Lucien_Davis%2C_1898.jpg/500px-Rowing%2C_Lucien_Davis%2C_1898.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Rowing%2C_Lucien_Davis%2C_1898.jpg/500px-Rowing%2C_Lucien_Davis%2C_1898.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Rowing, by Lucien Davis, 1898.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARowing%2C_Lucien_Davis%2C_1898.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Britannia_Yacht_Club_regatta_1895.jpg/500px-Britannia_Yacht_Club_regatta_1895.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Britannia_Yacht_Club_regatta_1895.jpg/500px-Britannia_Yacht_Club_regatta_1895.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Britannia Boating Clu